// Extending other definitions from outside their files, the way another pack
// adds to this one. First: an option for Wren's talk menu
// (characters/wren.fsc) from outside her file. Another pack can extend this
// pack's content the same way, without copying it. Replacing a field needs
// "== replace <type> <id>" instead.
== extend menu wren.talk
* The cabin -- Ask about your cabin
    'Old Tomas built it,' Wren says. 'He left one spring and never came back. It's yours now, I suppose.'

// Adding exits to a place from outside its file, as another pack would: a new
// place east of the old bridge. The way back is written on the new place.
== extend location old_bridge
exits:
    east: hollow_log

== location hollow_log
name: Hollow Log
region: woods
zone: riverbank
map: 4, 4
items: smooth_pebble, smooth_pebble
exits:
    west: old_bridge
description:
    A fallen oak, hollow from end to end, big enough to crawl through. Someone has left a row of smooth pebbles along its top.

